    {
      "key": 1,
      "pattern": "pat-verification-gap",
      "thesis": "The Verification Gap",
      "brief": "Generation has industrialized; verification has not. Agents ship 10× faster at worse defect rates (backlogs +108% QoQ despite tooling), and the generating model cannot validate itself (~50% repeat-find rate, ~40% F1 vs deterministic checks). Trust is therefore being re-architected outside the model: independent deterministic validators wired into the agent loop, runtime policy enforcement at the tool-call boundary (steer, don't ask), and a new role — the AI security engineer. Verification, not generation, becomes the bottleneck and the value layer.",
