      "key": 4,
      "pattern": "pat-benchmark-trust-crisis",
      "thesis": "The Benchmark Trust Crisis",
      "brief": "Benchmarks are decoupling from real capability across many independent failure modes at once: reward-hacking and replay/determinism exploits (a blind replay script matches the frontier model; pass@k proved equal to replay success on deterministic envs), contamination, construction-methodology and reporting-threshold problems (METR 50% headline inflates capability ~5x read at 90-99% accuracy), simulation-awareness, purpose/profit drift, and task-distribution mismatch. The measurement the field steers by can certify memorization or vendor incentive rather than deployable capability; the antidote practitioners reach for is private, real-codebase re-run suites.",
